The regional transit agency says the areas with the biggest drops in ridership since 2001 - inner North and Northeast Portland - also reported some of the biggest increases in home prices. In most of those neighborhoods, prices doubled during that time frame.
Ridership, however, grew in farther flung areas - east of Interstate 205 and west of Beaverton, where housing prices are relatively low in a region where the median home costs about $385,000.
